  "body": "Per-source policy limits could accept missing, zero or negative values, and evidence receipts could contradict individually valid fetch/capture records. PR-009 now rejects those inconsistencies with typed results while preserving legitimate HTTP 304 reuse of an earlier capture and its original provenance.\n\n- Assignment: PR-009, P1 / 1C; R03/R14/R15/R16 and F03/F13/F32/F33. Bounded C-009-2 policy and C-009-3 receipt engineering. C-009-1 measured topology qualification remains unresolved under the adopted continuation scope.\n- Candidate: `27d0b0d7c31d8825b91d899dc280cd843af21465`, tree `aef0428057d73645fab00f4d3aecb3418296f79b`. Source correction: `ae9e54caa7298c7d53ba8900bc4ed65fc61f70b7`; the final commit retains its evidence and handoff.\n- Accepted/scoped local base: `b3fdf5f3145538c8316e0565a130b4c6987a000f`. This PR also carries the reviewed PR-006/008 acceptance evidence, PR086 continuation closure and PR009 scope adoption above published integration `8f2914e345b30809be4e1ad97cdccc39b809cc95`.\n- Dependency merges: PR-003 `c70b0790ca439d56bb2c9936d53837c6f68b6d57`; PR-004 `463f092f71c0ed1ef2aa5baa29b186e5697d04ce`; PR-007 `17f9271372ecdf29f6b818ad9caaa5332258f4fd`; PR-008 accepted bundle `8f2914e345b30809be4e1ad97cdccc39b809cc95`.\n- Behavior: enforce meaningful source limits and evidence-bearing retention durations; malformed policy containers return typed invalid results. Receipts bind source/route/capture identities, observation status, hashes, media and byte counts to their cited records. A 304 can retain a capture from an earlier run and connector version.\n- Compatibility: released ingestion/connector contracts, original nine tests and paused source policies are preserved. The named descriptor basis is `ushso-canonical-json.v1`; the receipt module does not establish registry approval or canonical digest equality. PR010 must resolve and verify the actual approved descriptor before admission.\n- Producer verification: `node --test tests/research-program/operating-bounds.test.mjs` passed 81/81; ADR audit passed. Astra independently replayed all 42 boundary cases (51 Node tests) on the final clean candidate, validated the default live-ledger handoff and passed 218 metadata integrity checks.\n- Full exact-candidate gate: all ten stages passed on the first attempt, with one build, in 564.751 seconds (run `20260912T132154Z-2104f3d6813f`). Astra rehashed all 41,869 retained artifacts; receipt SHA-256 `a24f44d56b31212ff7b9aa4465527b0d4e72dcd020f0b082292bc925b140278d`.\n- [Handoff](https://github.com/ajhcs/ushso/blob/27d0b0d7c31d8825b91d899dc280cd843af21465/docs/research-program/handoffs/PR-009.json), [retained correction evidence](https://github.com/ajhcs/ushso/tree/27d0b0d7c31d8825b91d899dc280cd843af21465/verification/research-program/pr-009/successor-correction-20260912), and [adopted scope](https://github.com/ajhcs/ushso/blob/27d0b0d7c31d8825b91d899dc280cd843af21465/docs/master-plan/2026-09-10/prs/PR-009.md) retain exact identity and artifact hashes. Initial 22 boundary failures and four malformed-policy failures remain historical evidence. The handoff-ID rejection and corrected pass are retained in local review scratch.\n- Current limits: hosted CI and engineering integration pending. Numeric budget is owner-deferred; no measured-cheapest topology, source access, scientific approval, R01\u2013R16 acceptance or production qualification is claimed. Current activation remains disabled. PR010 continuation requires the actual accepted engineering merge and an explicit interface decision.\n- Review owner: Astra/root; implementation and publication payload review: native subagent. Rollback is the prior integration commit; no migration or production configuration change is included.\n",
